# TUI Reference

Complete reference for agent-deck Terminal UI features.

## Keyboard Shortcuts

### Navigation

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `j` / `↓` | Move down |
| `k` / `↑` | Move up |
| `h` / `←` | Collapse group / go to parent |
| `l` / `→` / `Tab` | Toggle expand/collapse group |
| `1-9` | Jump to Nth root group |

### Session Actions

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `Enter` | Attach to session OR toggle group |
| `n` | New session (inherits current group) |
| `r` | Rename session or group |
| `R` | Restart session (reloads MCPs) |
| `+` / `K` / `Shift+↑` | Move item up (auto-promotes a sub-session to top-level when at the parent's first child) |
| `-` / `J` / `Shift+↓` | Move item down (auto-promotes a sub-session to top-level when at the parent's last child) |
| `Shift+→` / `Shift+←` | Indent / outdent within current group (single-level nesting) |
| `M` | Move session to different group |
| `m` | Open MCP Manager (Claude/Gemini) |
| `s` | Open Skills Manager |
| `d` | Delete session or group |
| `A` | Archive session (stops tmux, hides from default list; conversations/metadata untouched) |
| `Shift+U` | Unarchive session (restores to list; does NOT auto-start tmux) |
| `b` | Re-run worktree setup script (`.agent-deck/worktree-setup.sh`) |
| `u` | Mark unread (idle -> waiting) |
| `f` | Quick fork (Claude/OpenCode/Pi/Codex) |
| `F` | Fork with options (Claude/OpenCode/Pi/Codex) |

For remote group headers, `Enter`/`Tab` toggles collapse and `h`/Left collapses or moves to the parent. Remote-session reorder keys move only within the current remote group; the order is saved on the viewing machine, while remote group headers remain name-sorted.

### Group Actions

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `g` | Create group (subgroup if on group) |
| `r` | Rename group |

### Search & Filter

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `/` | Local search (fuzzy) |
| `G` | Global search (all Claude conversations) |
| `Tab` | Switch between local/global search |
| `0` | Clear filter (show all) |
| `!` | Filter: running only (toggle) |
| `@` | Filter: waiting only (toggle) |
| `#` | Filter: idle only (toggle) |
| `$` | Filter: error only (toggle) |
| `^` | Filter: view archived sessions (toggle) |

### Global

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `?` | Help overlay |
| `i` | Import existing tmux sessions |
| `Ctrl+R` | Manual refresh |
| `Ctrl+Q` | Detach (keep tmux running) |
| `q` / `Ctrl+C` | Quit |

## Local Status Indicators

| Symbol | Status | Color | Meaning |
|--------|--------|-------|---------|
| `●` | Running | Green | Active, content changed in last 2s |
| `◐` | Waiting | Yellow | Stopped, unacknowledged |
| `○` | Idle | Gray | Stopped, acknowledged |
| `✕` | Error | Red | tmux session doesn't exist |
| `⟳` | Starting | Yellow | Session launching |

Federated remote rows currently carry coarse running/waiting/idle/error status; local Honest Status substates are not included in the remote payload.

## Dialogs

### New Session (`n`)

**Fields (order: Name → Tool → Path):**
- Session name (required)
- Command (claude/gemini/opencode/codex/custom) — the dialog remembers the last-used tool (persisted per profile, never written to config.toml; an explicit `default_tool` in config wins)
- Project path (required, supports `~/`)
- Parent group (auto-selected)
- Claude options (when Claude is selected): permission mode, Chrome, teammate mode, extra args, and start query

**Controls:** `Tab` move fields | `Enter` advance to next field (on free-text Name/Branch fields) | `Ctrl+S` create from any field | `Esc` cancel

Enter-advances is the default (`[ui].new_session_enter_advances = true`), so typing a name and pressing Enter no longer silently creates a session with all defaults. Set `[ui].new_session_enter_advances = false` to restore the legacy Enter-submits behavior; `Ctrl+S` submits in both modes.

Pressing `n` on a remote group/session opens a remote-aware dialog (remote paths and group pre-filled); the session is created over SSH on the remote, never on localhost.

Claude New Session defaults are remembered in `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agent-deck/config.toml` (default `~/.config/agent-deck/config.toml`) under `[claude]`, except start query and resume IDs, which are per-launch values.

### MCP Manager (`m`)

**Layout:**
- Two columns: Attached | Available
- Two scopes: LOCAL | GLOBAL

**Controls:**
- `Tab` - Switch scope
- `←/→` - Switch columns
- `↑/↓` - Navigate
- `Type letters/digits` - Jump to MCP name prefix
- `Space` - Toggle MCP
- `Enter` - Apply changes
- `Esc` - Cancel

**Indicators:**
- `(l)` LOCAL scope
- `(g)` GLOBAL scope
- `(p)` PROJECT scope
- `🔌` MCP is pooled
- `⟳` Pending restart

### Skills Manager (`s`)

**Layout:**
- Two columns: Attached | Available
- Available is pool-only (`source=pool`)
- Column headers include counts (for example: `Attached (3)`, `Available (28)`)

**Controls:**
- `←/→` - Switch columns
- `↑/↓` - Navigate (scrolls long lists)
- `Type letters/digits` - Jump to skill name prefix
- `Space` - Move skill between columns
- `Enter` - Apply changes
- `Esc` - Cancel

**Persistence:**
- Writes attachment state to `<project>/.agent-deck/skills.toml`
- Claude-compatible sessions materialize selected entries in `<project>/.claude/skills`
- Gemini, Codex, and Pi sessions materialize selected entries in `<project>/.agents/skills`
- If no pool entries exist, dialog shows guidance for `~/.agent-deck/skills/pool`

**Runtime notes:**
- Skills Manager is available for Claude, Gemini, Codex, and Pi sessions
- Pressing `Enter` reconciles managed attachments to the active runtime root even if the attached list did not change
- Auto-restart after apply is supported for Claude, Gemini, and Codex; Pi requires manual reload/restart

### Fork Dialog (`F`)

**Fields:**
- Session title (pre-filled)
- Group (auto-selected)

**Controls:** `Enter` fork | `Esc` cancel

### Delete Confirmation (`d`)

**For sessions:** Warning about tmux kill, process termination

**For groups:** Sessions move to default (not deleted)

**Controls:** `y` confirm | `n`/`Esc` cancel

## Search

### Local Search (`/`)

- Fuzzy search session titles and groups
- Max 10 results
- `↑/↓` or `Ctrl+K/J` navigate
- `Enter` select | `Tab` switch to global | `Esc` close

### Global Search (`G`)

- Full content search across `~/.claude/projects/`
- Regex + fuzzy matching
- Recency ranking
- Split view: results + preview
- `[/]` scroll preview
- `Enter` create/jump to session

**Config:**
```toml
[global_search]
enabled = true
recent_days = 30
```

## Preview Pane

- Shows last ~500 lines of session's tmux pane
- Auto-updates every 2 seconds
- Launch animation: 6-15s for Claude/Gemini

## Layout

- **< 50 cols:** List only
- **50-79 cols:** Stacked (list above preview)
- **80+ cols:** Side-by-side (default)

## Tool Icons

| Tool | Icon | Color |
|------|------|-------|
| Claude | 🤖 | Orange |
| Gemini | ✨ | Purple |
| OpenCode | 🌐 | Cyan |
| Codex | 💻 | Cyan |
| Cursor | 📝 | Blue |
| Shell | 🐚 | Default |

## Color Scheme (Tokyo Night)

| Element | Color |
|---------|-------|
| Accent (selection) | #7aa2f7 |
| Running | #9ece6a |
| Waiting | #e0af68 |
| Error | #f7768e |
| Groups | #7dcfff |
| Background | #1a1b26 |
| Surface | #24283b |

## Hidden Features

- **`Ctrl+K/J`:** Vim-style navigation in search
- **Numbers 1-9:** Jump to root groups instantly
- **Status filters are toggles:** Press again to turn off
Agent Deck v1.14.0
Terminal session manager for AI coding agents

Usage: agent-deck [-p profile] [-g group] [--select id|title] [command]

Global Options:
  -p, --profile <name>   Use specific profile (default: 'default')
  -g, --group <name>     Launch TUI scoped to a specific group
  --select <id|title>    Launch TUI with cursor on a specific session (all groups stay visible)

Commands:
  (none)           Start the TUI
  add <path>       Add a new session
  launch [path]    Add, start, and optionally send a message in one step
  try <name>       Quick experiment (create/find dated folder + session)
  list, ls         List all sessions
  remove, rm       Remove a session
  rename, mv       Rename a session
  status           Show session status summary
  session          Manage session lifecycle
  fleet            Detect and recover from a fleet-wide session death
  mcp              Manage MCP servers
  skill            Manage project skills
  codex-hooks      Manage Codex notify hook integration
  gemini-hooks     Manage Gemini hook integration
  hermes-hooks     Manage Hermes Agent hook integration
  cursor-hooks     Manage Cursor Agent CLI hook integration
  deepseek         Inspect the DeepSeek Harness (dsh) integration
  group            Manage groups
  worktree, wt     Manage git worktrees
  web              Start TUI with web UI server running alongside
  remote           Manage remote agent-deck instances
  conductor        Manage conductor meta-agent orchestration
  telegram-doctor  Audit channel-owning sessions for telegram drops (#1138)
  profile          Manage profiles
  update           Check for and install updates
  debug-dump       Dump debug ring buffer to file for sharing
  migrate-paths    Copy legacy ~/.agent-deck files into XDG paths
  uninstall        Uninstall Agent Deck
  version          Show version
  help             Show this help

Session Commands:
  session start <id>        Start a session's tmux process
  session stop <id>         Stop session process
  session restart <id>      Restart session (reload MCPs)
  session fork <id>         Fork Claude or Pi session with context
  session attach <id>       Attach to session interactively
  session show [id]         Show session details

Fleet Recovery Commands:
  fleet status              Report sessions whose panes are gone (read-only)
  fleet recover             Plan a sequential recovery sweep (add --yes to run it)

MCP Commands:
  mcp list                  List available MCPs from config.toml
  mcp attached [id]         Show MCPs attached to a session
  mcp attach <id> <mcp>     Attach MCP to session
  mcp detach <id> <mcp>     Detach MCP from session

Skill Commands:
  skill list                List discoverable skills
  skill attached [id]       Show skills attached to a session
  skill attach <id> <name>  Attach skill to session project
  skill detach <id> <name>  Detach skill from session project
  skill source list         List global skill sources

Codex Hook Commands:
  codex-hooks install       Install or upgrade Codex notify hook
  codex-hooks uninstall     Remove Codex notify hook
  codex-hooks status        Show Codex hook install status
  gemini-hooks install      Install Gemini hooks
  gemini-hooks uninstall    Remove Gemini hooks
  gemini-hooks status       Show Gemini hooks install status
  hermes-hooks install      Install Hermes Agent hooks
  hermes-hooks uninstall    Remove Hermes Agent hooks
  hermes-hooks status       Show Hermes hooks install status
  cursor-hooks install      Install Cursor hooks
  cursor-hooks uninstall    Remove Cursor hooks
  cursor-hooks status       Show Cursor hooks install status
  deepseek status           Show resolved dsh binary, DSH_HOME, profile
  deepseek profiles         List profiles under $DSH_HOME/profiles
  deepseek sessions [path]  List dsh sessions recorded for a workspace

Group Commands:
  group list                List all groups
  group create <name>       Create a new group
  group delete <name>       Delete a group
  group move <id> <group>   Move session to group

Conductor Commands:
  conductor setup           Set up conductor (Telegram bridge + sessions)
  conductor teardown        Stop conductor and remove bridge daemon
  conductor status          Show conductor health across profiles
  conductor list            List configured conductors

Remote Commands:
  remote add <name> <user@host>             Register a remote agent-deck instance
    --agent-deck-path <path>                Path to agent-deck binary on remote (default: agent-deck)
    --profile <name>                        Remote profile to use (default: default)
  remote remove, rm <name>                  Remove a remote
  remote list, ls [--json]                  List configured remotes
  remote sessions [name] [--json]           Show sessions on remote(s)
  remote attach <name> <session>            Attach to a remote session
  remote rename <name> <session> <title>    Rename a remote session
  remote update [name]                      Install/upgrade agent-deck on remote(s)

Worktree Commands:
  worktree list             List worktrees with session associations
  worktree info <session>   Show worktree info for a session
  worktree cleanup          Find and remove orphaned worktrees/sessions

Profile Commands:
  profile list              List all profiles
  profile create <name>     Create a new profile
  profile delete <name>     Delete a profile
  profile default [name]    Show or set default profile

Examples:
  agent-deck                            # Start TUI with default profile
  agent-deck -p work                    # Start TUI with 'work' profile
  agent-deck add .                      # Add current directory
  agent-deck add -t "My App" -g dev .   # With title and group
  agent-deck session start my-project   # Start a session
  agent-deck session show               # Show current session (in tmux)
  agent-deck mcp list --json            # List MCPs as JSON
  agent-deck mcp attach my-app exa      # Attach MCP to session
  agent-deck skill attach my-app react  # Attach skill to project
  agent-deck group move my-app work     # Move session to group
  agent-deck web                        # TUI + web server on 127.0.0.1:8420
  agent-deck web --listen 127.0.0.1:9000  # TUI + web on a custom loopback port
  agent-deck web --read-only            # TUI + web in read-only mode
  agent-deck web --token secret         # auth token (REQUIRED to bind a non-loopback address)
  agent-deck web --help                 # Show web command flags

Environment Variables:
  AGENTDECK_PROFILE    Default profile to use
  AGENTDECK_COLOR      Color mode: truecolor, 256, 16, none

Configuration:
  Config file: /home/ashesh/.agent-deck/config.toml
  Since v1.9.49 config lives under the XDG base dirs, not ~/.agent-deck.
  Run 'agent-deck migrate-paths' to copy legacy ~/.agent-deck files across.

Keyboard shortcuts (in TUI):
  n          New session
  g          New group
  Enter      Attach to session
  m          MCP Manager
  s          Skills Manager
  M          Move session to group
  r          Rename session/group
  R          Restart session
  d          Delete session/group
  S          Settings
  /          Search
  Ctrl+Q     Detach from session
