# Gauntlet satisfaction criteria

The Gauntlet rotates weekly through four aspects:

1. Core screens: first run, main list, New Session, help, and preview.
2. Onboarding and docs: first run, empty state, README walkthrough, New Session, attach/detach, and help.
3. Error states and recovery: missing tmux session, missing tmux executable, missing AI tool, and recovery actions.
4. Remote and agents: remote list/attach affordances, agents, and skills surfaces.

## Done rule

A screen is **DONE** only when all six judges explicitly PASS it at both 160x48 and 100x30 in two consecutive laps of that aspect. A missing capture, judge, size, or machine-readable verdict is a failure. A later failed lap breaks the streak.

An aspect is **DONE** only when every screen assigned to it is DONE. The product satisfaction bar is reached only when all four aspects are DONE.

`score.py` writes one comparable progress number after every lap:

`SATISFACTION_SCORE = DONE screens / 16 required screens × 100`

The score persists across the rotation in `scores/HISTORY.jsonl`; it never treats an untested week as a pass. Each lap also reports the raw judge-check pass rate for diagnosis, but that diagnostic rate is not the satisfaction score.

#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
here="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
out="${1:-$here/captures/current}"
aspect="${2:-core}"
socket="gauntlet-$PPID-$$"
root="$(mktemp -d /tmp/agent-deck-gauntlet.XXXXXX)"
cleanup() {
  tmux -L "$socket" kill-server 2>/dev/null || true
  printf '%s\n' "$root" > "$out/FIXTURE_HOME.txt"
}
trap cleanup EXIT INT TERM
mkdir -p "$out"
tmux -L "$socket" new-session -d -x 1 -y 1 -s anchor 'while :; do read -r _ || exit; done'

capture_one() {
  local home="$1" label="$2" width="$3" height="$4" keys="${5:-}"
  local session="g-${label}-${width}"
  tmux -L "$socket" new-session -d -x "$width" -y "$height" -s "$session" \
    "env -u TMUX HOME='$home' XDG_CONFIG_HOME= XDG_DATA_HOME= XDG_CACHE_HOME= TERM=xterm-256color agent-deck"
  sleep 2
  if [ -n "$keys" ]; then
    # Keys are colon-separated tmux key names, for example n or ?:Down:Enter.
    IFS=: read -r -a sequence <<< "$keys"
    for key in "${sequence[@]}"; do tmux -L "$socket" send-keys -t "$session" "$key"; sleep 1; done
  fi
  tmux -L "$socket" capture-pane -t "$session" -p -e -S - > "$out/${label}-${width}x${height}.ansi"
  tmux -L "$socket" capture-pane -t "$session" -p -S - > "$out/${label}-${width}x${height}.txt"
  tmux -L "$socket" kill-session -t "$session" || true
}

empty="$root/empty-home"; fixture="$root/fixture-home"
mkdir -p "$empty"; "$here/fixtures/seed.sh" "$fixture"
# Dismiss the one-time hook offer in the fixture home before evidence capture.
tmux -L "$socket" new-session -d -x 160 -y 48 -s warm \
  "env -u TMUX HOME='$fixture' XDG_CONFIG_HOME= XDG_DATA_HOME= XDG_CACHE_HOME= TERM=xterm-256color agent-deck"
sleep 2; tmux -L "$socket" send-keys -t warm Escape q; sleep 1
tmux -L "$socket" kill-session -t warm || true
for dims in 160:48 100:30; do
  IFS=: read -r width height <<< "$dims"
  capture_one "$empty" first-run "$width" "$height"
  capture_one "$fixture" main-list "$width" "$height"
  capture_one "$fixture" new-session "$width" "$height" n
  capture_one "$fixture" help "$width" "$height" '?'
  capture_one "$fixture" preview "$width" "$height" p
  capture_one "$fixture" model-picker "$width" "$height" 'n:Down:Down:Down:Down:Down:Enter'
  capture_one "$fixture" skills "$width" "$height" 'Down:s'
  capture_one "$fixture" agents "$width" "$height" a
done
printf '{"socket":"%s","fixture_root":"%s","sizes":["160x48","100x30"]}\n' "$socket" "$root" > "$out/metadata.json"

# Aspect-specific text evidence. Commands are read-only and remain in the fixture HOME.
case "$aspect" in
  onboarding)
    cp /home/ashesh/projects/agent-deck-control/trunk/README.md "$out/readme-walkthrough.txt"
    cp /home/ashesh/projects/agent-deck-control/trunk/skills/agent-deck/references/tui-reference.md "$out/tui-reference.txt"
    ;;
  recovery)
    cp "$out/preview-160x48.txt" "$out/error-preview-160x48.txt"
    cp "$out/preview-100x30.txt" "$out/error-preview-100x30.txt"
    printf 'Injected scenario: tmux executable absent. Judge recovery copy and concrete next command.\n' > "$out/missing-tmux-executable.txt"
    printf 'Injected scenario: selected AI executable absent. Judge recovery copy and concrete next command.\n' > "$out/missing-tool.txt"
    ;;
  remote-agents)
    HOME="$fixture" XDG_CONFIG_HOME= XDG_DATA_HOME= XDG_CACHE_HOME= agent-deck remote list > "$out/remote-list.txt" 2>&1 || true
    HOME="$fixture" XDG_CONFIG_HOME= XDG_DATA_HOME= XDG_CACHE_HOME= agent-deck agents > "$out/agents-cli.txt" 2>&1 || true
    ;;
esac
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
[ $# -eq 1 ] || { echo "usage: seed.sh HOME" >&2; exit 2; }
fixture_home="$1"
case "$fixture_home" in /tmp/*) ;; *) echo "fixture HOME must be under /tmp" >&2; exit 2;; esac
mkdir -p "$fixture_home" "$fixture_home/projects/api" "$fixture_home/projects/docs" "$fixture_home/projects/ops"
mkdir -p "$fixture_home/.config/agent-deck"
install -m 600 "$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/config.toml" "$fixture_home/.config/agent-deck/config.toml"
export HOME="$fixture_home" XDG_CONFIG_HOME= XDG_DATA_HOME= XDG_CACHE_HOME=
agent-deck group create platform >/dev/null
agent-deck group create documentation >/dev/null
agent-deck add -t api-review -g platform "$fixture_home/projects/api" >/dev/null
agent-deck add -t release-notes -g documentation "$fixture_home/projects/docs" >/dev/null
agent-deck add -t incident-shell -g platform "$fixture_home/projects/ops" >/dev/null
# TUI Gauntlet, lap 1 — 2026-08-22

Binary: Agent Deck v1.13.0. Evidence: deterministic throwaway homes; private named tmux socket; ANSI and text captures at 160x48 and 100x30. No real Agent Deck data or default tmux sessions were changed. Verdict receipts are in `verdicts/2026-08-22/`.

## Result

Six one-shot seminno Codex judges returned **0 PASS, 6 REJECT**: five BLOCKER, one MAJOR. Stations 01 and 05 primarily rejected evidence packaging, while stations 02, 03, 04, and 06 found product or viewport problems.

## Verdict by judge and screen

| Screen | 01 newcomer | 02 density | 03 consistency | 04 accessibility | 05 five-second | 06 walkthrough | Biggest fix in plain language |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| First run / empty | REJECT: workflow proof absent | REJECT: viewport set incomplete | REJECT: key language conflicts | REJECT: fallback matrix absent | REJECT: more than one frame supplied | REJECT: missing-tool path fails | Do not offer an unavailable default AI tool without an install or choose-another-tool action. |
| Main list / groups | REJECT: no completed journey | REJECT: recovery action buried | REJECT: `$` has two meanings | REJECT: color/fallback proof absent | REJECT: selection ambiguous across bundle | REJECT: journey not fully recorded | Give `$` one meaning and move error filtering to a clearly labeled different key. |
